---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const presets = [
 ['overworld','Overworld','A familiar place to get lost.','01'],
  ['chess','Infinite chess','Your next move, anywhere.','02'],
  ['rpg','RPG overworld','Take the long way home.','03'],
  ['hell','Hell world','Some like it very, very hot.','04'],
  ['islands','Islands','One more shore to explore.','05'],
  ['sky-islands','Sky islands','Mind the gap.','06'],
  ['ocean','Ocean world','A little land goes a long way.','07'],
  ['arena','Arena','A fair place to settle things.','08'],
  ['maze','Maze','There is a way through.','09'],
  ['moon','Cratered moon','A quiet place beyond home.','10'],
  ['wetlands','Mushroom wetlands','Something strange is growing.','11'],
];
---
<Layout>
<main id="main">
<section class="hero page-width">
<div class="eyebrow">
<span class="status-dot">
</span>OPEN SOURCE WORLD GENERATION</div>
<h1>A whole world.<br/>
<span>A little JSON.</span>
</h1>
<p class="hero-description">Give it a seed. Get a world.<br class="mobile-break"/> Terrain, biomes, and things to discover.<br/>You bring the game.</p>
<div class="hero-actions">
<a class="button primary" href="#playground">Make yourself a world <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span>
</a>
<a class="text-link" href="/docs">Read the docs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
</a>
</div>
<div class="hero-caption">
<span>Deterministic by design</span>
<span>No keys. No accounts.</span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="playground" class="playground page-width" aria-labelledby="playground-title">
<div class="section-top">
<div>
<span class="eyebrow">A SMALL WINDOW INTO SOMETHING BIG</span>
<h2 id="playground-title">Go on, explore.</h2>
</div>
<span class="live-label">
<span class="status-dot">
</span>Interactive playground</span>
</div>
<div class="world-workbench">
<div class="world-toolbar">
<form id="world-form">
<label>World<select id="preset" name="preset">{presets.map(([id,name])=>
<option value={id}>{name}</option>)}</select>
</label>
<label class="seed-label">Seed<div class="seed-input">
<input id="seed" name="seed" value="hello-world" maxlength="128" required spellcheck="false"/>
<button type="button" id="shuffle" aria-label="Choose a random seed" title="Choose a random seed">⤨</button>
</div>
</label>
<button class="button primary generate-button" id="generate" type="submit">Generate <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
</button>
</form>
<div class="layer-control">
<label for="layer">View</label>
<select id="layer">
<option value="biome">Biomes</option>
<option value="elevation">Elevation</option>
<option value="objects">Objects</option>
</select>
</div>
</div>
<details class="world-settings">
<summary>Customize this world <span>Terrain &amp; window</span>
</summary>
<div class="settings-grid">
<label>Terrain scale<input id="terrain-scale" type="number" min="4" max="4096" value="128" form="world-form" required/>
</label>
<label>Sea level<input id="sea-level" type="number" min="0" max="65535" value="28000" form="world-form" required/>
</label>
<label>Roughness<input id="roughness" type="number" min="0" max="1" step="0.05" value="0.35" form="world-form" required/>
</label>
<label>Window X<input id="window-x" type="number" min="0" max="9007199254740990" value="0" form="world-form" required/>
</label>
<label>Window Y<input id="window-y" type="number" min="0" max="9007199254740990" value="0" form="world-form" required/>
</label>
<label>Window size<select id="window-size">
<option value="32">32 × 32</option>
<option value="64">64 × 64</option>
<option value="128" selected>128 × 128</option>
<option value="256">256 × 256</option>
</select>
</label>
</div>
<p>Changes apply when you generate. <a href="/docs#placement">Add placement rules through the API ↗</a>
</p>
</details>
<div class="canvas-wrap" id="canvas-wrap">
<canvas id="world-canvas" tabindex="0" role="img" aria-label="Interactive world map. Drag to pan, use plus and minus to zoom, and arrow keys to move.">
</canvas>
<div class="map-label">
<span class="status-dot">
</span>
<span id="map-title">Overworld</span>
<span class="map-label-separator">/</span>
<span id="map-seed">hello-world</span>
</div>
<div class="map-hint">Drag to explore <span>·</span> Scroll to zoom</div>
<div class="zoom-controls">
<button id="zoom-in" aria-label="Zoom in">+</button>
<button id="zoom-out" aria-label="Zoom out">−</button>
<button id="reset-view" aria-label="Reset map view" title="Reset view">⌖</button>
</div>
<div id="map-loading" class="map-loading">Growing a little world…</div>
</div>
<div class="world-status">
<span id="world-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading bundled world…</span>
<span id="cell-inspector">128 × 128 cells <span class="desktop-only">· 16 × 16 chunks</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="world-error" class="world-error" role="alert" hidden>
</div>
</div>
<div class="playground-footnote">
<p>Start with a ready-made world. Change the seed to make it yours.</p>
<div class="world-export-actions">
<button class="text-link" id="download-world">Download JSON <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></button>
<button class="text-link" id="copy-world-request">Copy this request <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
</button>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="presets-section page-width" aria-labelledby="presets-title">
<div class="section-top">
<div>
<span class="eyebrow">SOMEWHERE TO START</span>
<h2 id="presets-title">Different worlds. Same little API.</h2>
</div>
<p>Pick a preset. Bend the rules.<br/>See where you end up.</p>
</div>
<div class="preset-grid">{presets.map(([id,name,description,number])=>
<button class="preset-card" data-preset={id}>
<div class="preset-preview">
<canvas data-preview={id} width="192" height="112" aria-hidden="true">
</canvas>
<span class="preset-number">{number}</span>
<span class="preset-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
</div>
<div class="preset-copy">
<h3>{name}</h3>
<p>{description}</p>
</div>
</button>)}</div>
</section>
<section class="how-section page-width">
<div class="how-heading">
<span class="eyebrow">LESS SETUP, MORE PLAY</span>
<h2>Your world is<br/>one request away.</h2>
<p>A seed, a preset, a window. Get elevation, biomes, and placed objects as JSON. Render it however you like.</p>
<a class="text-link" href="/docs#quickstart">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
</a>
</div>
<div class="code-panel">
<div class="code-header">
<span>
<span class="method">QUERY</span> /api/world</span>
<button class="copy-code" data-copy="quickstart-code">Copy</button>
</div><pre id="quickstart-code"><code is:raw>curl --request QUERY \
  https://microworld.kaf.sh/api/world \
  --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  --data '{
    "seed": "hello-world",
    "preset": "overworld",
    "window": {
      "x": 0, "y": 0,
      "width": 128, "height": 128
    }
  }'</code></pre><div class="code-footer">Your seed. Your coordinates. The same world, every time.</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="principles page-width">
<article>
<span class="feature-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⌖</span>
<h3>A world that stays put.</h3>
<p>Request any window in any order. Versioned generation keeps terrain and placements consistent across chunk boundaries.</p>
</article>
<article>
<span class="feature-symbol" aria-hidden="true">▦</span>
<h3>Make the rules.</h3>
<p>Shape the terrain. Choose where things grow. Place structures with tile templates, spacing, and biome constraints.</p>
</article>
<article>
<span class="feature-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
<h3>Yours to build on.</h3>
<p>A public API and stateless MCP endpoint. Apache 2.0 source. Store your changes, bring your renderer, make something fun.</p>
</article>
</section>
<section class="closing page-width">
<span class="eyebrow">WHAT WILL YOU MAKE?</span>
<h2>Every good adventure<br/>starts somewhere.</h2>
<a class="button primary" href="/docs">Start building <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
</a>
<a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/iamkaf/microworld">Or help us grow Microworld ↗</a>
</section>
</main><script>import '../client/playground.ts';</script></Layout>
